        "args": {
          "content": "{\n  \"module\": \"packages/excalidraw/lasso\",\n  \"verdict\": \"needs_changes\",\n  \"tool_calls\": 29,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"packages/excalidraw/tests/selection.test.tsx\",\n      \"line\": 1465,\n      \"issue\": \"In describe(\\\"lasso selection mode\\\"), setup() renders <Excalidraw /> without setting non-zero viewport dimensions (h.state.width and h.state.height), so after restoreOriginalGetBoundingClientRect() runs in an earlier suite (line 1142), h.state.width and h.state.height default to 0 in jsdom and Renderer.getVisibleCanvasElements (isElementInViewport) culls every element whose bounds do not contain (0, 0) from h.app.visibleElements (specifically rect2 at x: 100 and child at x: 50, y: 20), causing LassoTrail.updateSelection() to never see those elements in the 3 failing pointer-driven tests.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Set h.state.width = 1000 and h.state.height = 1000 inside the act(() => { ... }) block in setup() (matching packages/excalidraw/tests/lasso.test.tsx lines 47-48) so all scene elements in the suite lie within the viewport and are included in h.app.visibleElements before API.setElements() and pointer lasso strokes run.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"refinement_packets\": []\n}"
